{#
  map_risk.j2
  ===========
  Verbal reading of the annual probability-of-infection map for one scenario.

  Context variables (from _build_map_risk_ctx):
    available       False when the scenario has no QMRA output
    r               the flattened QMRA metrics (analytics.build_narrative_scenario)
    top_areas, top_area_names, area_count, spread, route_label, quantile
#}
{% if available %}
The map below shows the modelled annual probability of infection{% if quantile %}, evaluated at the {{ quantile }} quantile of the exposure distribution{% endif %}. Every modelled exposure route is combined, so a single cell represents the total risk a person living there carries over a year.

{% if route_label %}
Exposure through {{ route_label }} contributes most to that combined risk.
{% endif %}
{% if r.risk_peak_month %}
Risk is highest in {{ r.risk_peak_month }} and lowest in {{ r.risk_trough_month }}, following the seasonal pattern of the concentrations.
{% endif %}

{% if top_areas %}
Risk is unevenly spread across the {{ area_count }} reporting areas{% if spread %}: the most affected area carries a probability of infection {{ spread | num }} times higher than the lowest-ranked area listed here{% endif %}. The most affected areas are:

{% for row in top_areas %}
- **{{ row.name }}**: annual probability of infection {{ row.risk | sci }}{% if row.cases %}, around {{ row.cases | sci }} expected infections per year{% endif %}{{ "" }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
